# nodus/oevm/tests/target/porta-refuse.env — rete#232, the gate #199 could not have
#
# A C6 pointed at a porta that answers #err to every datagram, watched past the
# longest recorded death on this bench. THE HOST CANNOT ANSWER THE DEATH QUESTION:
# it ran 300 s clean at the same arena size where the C6 died in 157 s — a 64-bit
# host never asks for 4 KB at the wrong moment — so `196ff1c`'s fix (frame reuse;
# GC cycles/tick 1.82 -> 0.42) was, until this scenario, an inference from a
# metric, and improvement is not a fix.
#
# `ref` CLIMBING IS THE PASS. A refused node that stays alive with `ref` rising is
# the property; a node that goes quiet is the FAIL. The TAPs only prove the
# injector refused us (a porta-refuse run against no injector, or against a porta
# that ANSWERS, must fail loudly, not score a survived run that tested nothing);
# the observation window is the verdict, as everywhere since rete#216.
#
# PRECONDITION — the refusing porta. The harness never reaches into a gateway; the
# injector is a SECOND porta instance the operator starts beside the real one,
# same host (the mesh-local EID the node dials is gw85224-01's), one UDP port up,
# throwaway db, refusing at the door (rete#232's --test-refuse-all — nothing is
# decoded or ingested, matching #199's witnessed reject-at-decode):
#
#   ssh gw85224-01 'cd ~/porta-v2 && nohup ./porta serve --udp :16971 \
#       --http-port 0 --db /tmp/porta-refuse-232.db --test-refuse-all \
#       > /tmp/porta-refuse-232.log 2>&1 & echo pid $!'
#
# Stop it by the echoed pid when the run is done (kill <pid> — NEVER a pattern
# pkill on this host). The real gateway on :6969 is untouched throughout.
#
# OBSERVE_S=240, derived not felt: the death record is 157 s measured from the
# FIRST CHECK-IN (#199's node died 46 ticks after its first exchange). The TAPs
# here pass ~30 s after refusal begins (refusedFloor 15 at the 2 s cadence), so
# 240 s of window watches past ~270 s of continuous refusal — comfortably beyond
# the record. Re-open this number when a death outlives it.
#
# CLASS=disruptive: this scenario is DESIGNED to kill the node if #199's fix is
# inadequate — an arena death inside the window is precisely what it exists to
# catch. Disposable board only.
#
# The two side questions this run can answer for free (#232): a death names its
# fatal allocation size in the GC error line (is it still 4104?), and a refusal a
# LATER frame would have satisfied is what would earn the deferred forced-rebuild
# tunable — both read from the log, neither is instrumented for.
SCENARIO=porta-refuse
NODE=RefusedProbeC6.nsl
BOARD_ID=esp32c6
CONF_EXTRA="prj_esp32c6_thread.conf;prj_esp32c6_thread_ftd.conf"
CLASS=disruptive
# Attach can eat 90 s before the first exchange; the workload emits its verdict
# at latest 240 s of ticking (verdictTicks 120 at 2 s), so 300 s bounds a run
# that has already decided.
TIMEOUT_S=300

OBSERVE_S=240
# The node's own per-cadence line (` ref N` rides after misses, so the log shows
# refusal climbing while the node stays alive). Positive predicate: #199's death
# is silent — no fault, no panic banner until the GC error — so absence of this
# line is the failure signal.
OBSERVE_PROGRESS='^.*tick [0-9]+ misses'
